==English==
{{Wikiquote}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ar|حَدِيث||Prophetic tradition}}, from {{m|ar|حَدَّثَ||to tell, relate, report}}.
{{root|en|ar|ح د ث}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|[həˈdiːθ]}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hadith.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|hadith|s|ahadith}}

# {{lb|en|countable|religion|Islam}} An [[eyewitness]] [[account]] of a [[saying]] or [[action]] of [[Muhammad]] or [[sometimes]] one of his [[companions]] not [[otherwise]] [[found]] in the [[Quran]].
#: {{ux|en|In addition to the Quran, Muslims also look to the '''hadiths''' for moral and spiritual guidance in their daily lives.}}
#: {{ux|en|There are four main Shia books of '''hadith''' and six main Sunni books of '''hadith'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|in the plural|religion|Islam}} A [[particular]] [[accepted]] [[collection]] of [[such]] [[account]]s, as from a [[single]] [[source]] or within a [[particular]] [[branch]] of [[Islam]] or [[Islam]]ic [[jurisprudence]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|uncountable}} the [[Hadith]], the [[Sunna]]
* {{sense|countable}} {{l|en|tradition}}, {{l|en|saying}}, {{l|en|deed}}, etc.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|hadithic}}

====Related terms====
* {{sense|adj.}} hadith, [[hadithic]], [[Hadithic]]
* {{l|en|Sunna}}

